content.text:
After 4.5 more (total ~5.7), job still 6 and packages true; timer maybe not fired due low frame rate? `setTimeout` should fire regardless. Wait the completeContract else:
```
setTimeout(() => {
 if (!playing || campaignComplete) return;
 job++; startContract...
}, 5200);
```
Ah! We return if campaignComplete, so in free roam, no automatic next contract. That's a bug: after campaign complete, clicking KEEP ROAMING starts job 6, but completing it sets missionDone and never starts another contract. Need fix: only return if final win; in free roam always start next. Change condition to `if (!playing) return;` and for campaign complete start next fine. But during final win, we don't schedule else. For final, separate return. So the `campaignComplete` guard is wrong. Remove it. Then free roam loops after 5.2s. Good. Also showToast "NEW CONTRACT · JOB 07 / 05" awkward; need adjust for free roam. Use label:
```
const label = campaignComplete ? 'FREE ROAM · CONTRACT ' + pad(job) : 'JOB ' + pad(job) + ' / 05';
showToast('NEW CONTRACT · ' + label)
```
And HUD label free roam. Let's patch.

