Now add event spots, beacon, state after packages/extraction. Find lines around `const extractBeacon...`. We'll insert after `extraction = { x: 234, z: 0 };`.

Define:
```
const EVENT_SPOTS = [...]
const streetBeacon = makeBeacon(0xffc35e); streetBeacon.visible=false; world.add(streetBeacon);
const streetEvent = { active:false, ... };
let eventCooldown = 0;
```
Need `makeBeacon` defined before yes. `makeBeacon` uses flat. okay.

EVENT_SPOTS must avoid collisions; choose intersections. All coordinates multiples of 78 plus 39? Road coords are -234,-156,-78,0,78,156,234. City blocks centers at -195,-117,-39,39,117,195, with buildings w ~41-51, so building edge from center 20-25. Road at 78, building at 39 edge to ~64, clear. Intersections (78,0) etc are open. Use road coords only, not block centers. But if spot at intersection x=0,z=78 is road crossing; fine. Additional road midpoints e.g. x=39,z=78 is on horizontal road at 78 and block center x39? x=39 is block center, z=78 road; that's road. Fine. But use intersections.

```
const EVENT_SPOTS = [
 {x:-156,z:0},{x:-78,z:0},{x:0,z:0},{x:78,z:0},{x:156,z:0},
 {x:0,z:-156},{x:0,z:-78},{x:0,z:78},{x:0,z:156},
 {x:-156,z:78},{x:156,z:78},{x:-156,z:-78},{x:156,z:-78},{x:78,z:156},{x:-78,z:156},{x:78,z:-156},{x:-78,z:-156}
];
```
Spot (0,0) is player start; if event spawns there maybe too easy; filter distance > 45. good.

Street event object fields. Let's patch.

